# Repository invariant (operator rule of 2026-09-29; organization layer 1.16.0). Layer: situated.
"@context": "urn:bedrock:context/v1"
"@id": "urn:bedrock:vertex/invariant-public-secure-material"
"@type": "urn:bedrock:ontology/Invariant"
label: "Public secure-material boundary"
layer: "situated"
statement: >
  This repository is public. Secure material — our own known vulnerabilities
  from the security vault, their details, exploitability and affected code
  paths — is never represented in it: not in code, comments, commits,
  branches, issues, pull requests, reviews or comments. Public CVE and CWE
  references are fine. A fix lands normally, with a Promise that describes the
  property the code keeps, never the vulnerability.
